Under the Act of Congress (10 USC 1362), the DACS was empowered to provide funding assistance for federally funded research projects, which have been initiated or approved under the Federal Government's authority. While the act of Congress does not specifically authorize federal agencies to make grants to states or localities, it does authorize the DACS to receive funds from the U.S. Treasury to conduct certain types of research, such as:
- Research into wildlife and endangered species;
- Development of new technologies;
- Research into natural resources;
- Research into the use of explosives and explosives in warfare;
- Work on the development of nuclear weapons and materials;
- Work with foreign governments to develop military and commercial bases;
- Work with other federal agencies to undertake public works and activities
